# Template for ops/.env.docker (sandbox/dev only). Copy it to ops/.env.docker
# and fill in real values there; ops/.env.docker is gitignored and must never
# be committed. Use the hosting platform's secret store for deployed values.
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000

# Acquirer sandbox callback signing secret. Get it from the acquirer
# integration contact or your secret store.
ACQUIRER_CALLBACK_SIGNING_SECRET=replace-me

# Browser sites allowed to call the API (D4), comma-separated. With
# NODE_ENV=production the default is none, so the dashboard (:5173) and ops
# console (:5174) would be blocked. These are local-testing values only: the
# deployed URLs aren't known yet; set the real web and admin origins on the
# deployment server.
# Note: ops/docker-compose.yml has no env_file, so compose does NOT pass this
# file into the containers (checked with `docker compose config`); the
# api container runs in development mode, where these two origins are
# already the default. This file only takes effect where something loads it.
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:5174
